questions.question_text:
A continuous random variable has $f(x) = 0.2$ for $0 \le x < 2$ and $f(x) = 0.3$ for $2 \le x \le 4$, and $0$ elsewhere.
Find $F(x)$ for $2 \le x \le 4$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, x=1.0cm, y=6cm]
\draw[->] (-0.6,0) -- (5.4,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[->] (0,-0.08) -- (0,0.45) node[above] {$f(x)$};
\draw[thick] (-0.5,0) -- (0,0);
\draw[thick] (0,0.2) -- (2,0.2);
\draw[thick] (2,0.3) -- (4,0.3);
\draw[dashed] (0,0.2) -- (0,0);
\draw[dashed] (2,0.2) -- (2,0.3);
\draw[dashed] (4,0.3) -- (4,0);
\draw[thick] (4,0) -- (5.2,0);
\node[left] at (0,0.2) {$0.2$};
\node[left] at (0,0.3) {$0.3$};
\node[below] at (2,0) {$2$};
\node[below] at (4,0) {$4$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
